or-owned summary route, conflating the SDK retry layer with this app-layer wrapper."],"finding":"The plan neutralizes only the Jira DC SDK retry (jira.JIRA max_retries=0) but does not address the adapter's own app-layer retry wrapper _with_connection_retry, a second independent retry loop (up to 3 attempts, 2s then 5s backoff, per retry.py) that every DC transport method routes through, including the summary write.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdedc29e52b23352a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 6; Scope (Jira DC transport.py, retry.py, _issues.py)","norm_id":"n22420e723674bda9","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A summary write on DC hits a connection-level fault; _with_connection_retry sleeps 2s+5s and re-runs the write inside a single 'physical invocation', silently double-sleeping and replaying beneath the executor budget the plan claims is the sole owner."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In step 6 and Scope, specify that for the executor-owned summary route the _IssuesMixin.update_issue write path bypasses _with_connection_retry's attempt loop (or calls it with a single-attempt/no-sleep policy), so the shared budget is the only layer that retries or sleeps on DC.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site",